Using the values of $a$ and $b$ found in Sub-problem-Id: 1, we can evaluate $(a-1)(b-1)$:

\begin{align*}
(a-1)(b-1) &= \left(\frac{7}{4}-\frac{\sqrt{33}}{4}\right)\left(\frac{\sqrt{33}}{4}+\frac{7}{4}\right)\\
&= \frac{49}{16}-\frac{7\sqrt{33}}{16} + \frac{7\sqrt{33}}{16} - \frac{33}{16}\\
&= \frac{1}{16}
\end{align*}

Now, we can evaluate $a+b-2$:

$$a+b-2 = \left(\frac{7}{4}-\frac{\sqrt{33}}{4}\right) + \left(\frac{\sqrt{33}}{4}+\frac{7}{4}\right)-2 = \frac{7}{2}$$

Therefore, we have:

$$\frac{1}{a-1} + \frac{1}{b-1} = \frac{a+b-2}{(a-1)(b-1)} = \frac{\frac{7}{2}}{\frac{1}{16}} = \boxed{112}$$
